  8 => [
    'transcript' => 'Speaker 1: The curriculum committee is proposing that every student, regardless of their major, complete one full year of a foreign language course before graduating. They say it\'s about producing more globally minded graduates, and they want our thoughts before it goes to a formal vote.
Speaker 2: I actually really support this. Learning another language isn\'t just about communication, it also has documented cognitive benefits, like improved problem-solving and multitasking ability. Plus, in an increasingly global job market, having even basic proficiency in a second language can set graduates apart when they\'re applying for international roles.
Speaker 3: I see the value, but making it compulsory for absolutely everyone seems excessive. Students in highly technical fields like engineering or computer science already have packed schedules, and squeezing in a mandatory language course could push out electives that are actually more relevant to their career path. Also, some students are already multilingual and would find a beginner course pointless.
